  "description_short": "Family-run wine estate in The Crags offering locally-made wines, craft beer, and relaxed country lunches.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into the hills of The Crags between Plettenberg Bay and Nature's Valley, Bramon Wine Estate is a working farm where you can taste locally produced wines and craft beers alongside generous country-style meals. The tasting room and restaurant overlook the vineyards, with mountain views stretching across the indigenous forest beyond. It's the kind of place where you linger over a cheese platter and a bottle of their MCC, watching the light change across the valley.\n\nThe menu leans into fresh, honest cooking — think wood-fired pizzas, seasonal salads, and platters designed for sharing. Bramon grows their own grapes and hops on-site, and that farm-to-table ethos comes through in everything they serve. It's popular with families on weekend outings and couples looking for a quieter alternative to the beachfront buzz. Book ahead during peak season, especially if you want a table on the lawn.",
